From f5301dba45c7f13eb36f62e567b48528bc5b585e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen De Vleeschauwer <kdv@kdvelectronics.eu>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:16:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] weact-u585: Add the WeAct Black Pill STM32U585 platform

A BMPv3-derived platform for the WeAct Black Pill STM32U585 core board
(STM32U585CIU6, UFQFPN48), with the pinout following the board's CubeMX
project: JTAG/SWD and the external SPI bus on PB12-PB15, open drain nRST
on PA15, SWO on PA1, AUX UARTs on PA2/PA3 and PA9/PA10, the internal SPI
bus on SPI1 (PA4-PA7, U3 Flash footprint) and the user LED on PC13.

Clocks are as on BMPv3. The 25MHz HSE and 32.768kHz LSE crystals are
started at boot; a crystal that does not start is signalled by blinking
the LED (3 times for the HSE, 2 times for the LSE) before carrying on.

There is no BMD bootloader: the firmware runs from 0x08000000 and
BOOT0 + NRST or a DFU detach enters the ST ROM DFU bootloader.

The debug pins use low GPIO speed: unlike BMPv3 they drive the target
wiring directly, and faster edges ring on jumper wires.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
