@@ -0,0 +1,83 @@
+# Black Magic Debug firmware for the WeAct Black Pill STM32U585
+
+*Written by Claude (Anthropic's AI model) during development with Koen De Vleeschauwer. Not reviewed line by
+line.*
+
+This platform runs Black Magic Debug on a
+[WeAct Black Pill STM32U585 core board](https://github.com/WeActStudio/WeActStudio.STM32U585Cx_CoreBoard)
+(STM32U585CIU6, UFQFPN48). It is derived from the BMPv3 platform, with the pinout following the board's
+CubeMX project.
+
+This is not an official Black Magic Debug platform.
+
+## Features and limitations
+
+- JTAG and SWD on the board headers, as direct GPIO with no level translators: 3.3V targets only
+- SWO capture on PA1, Manchester and UART/NRZ encodings
+- Two AUX UARTs on one USB serial port; the port follows whichever UART sees activity
+- Internal SPI bus to the U3 Flash footprint, for `bmpflash`. U3 is not fitted on stock boards;
+  a W25Q128JV has been tested
+- External SPI bus on the JTAG pins, for programming a target's SPI Flash with `bmpflash`
+- No target power switch and no target voltage sense (`Target voltage: Unknown`)
+- No BMD bootloader: the firmware sits at `0x08000000` and the ST ROM DFU bootloader is used for updates
+- Single user LED (PC13) for the idle/run, error and UART activity indications
+
+## Clocks
+
+SYSCLK is 160MHz from PLL1 fed by MSIS and USB runs from HSI48 trimmed against USB SOF by the CRS,
+exactly as on BMPv3. The board's 25MHz HSE and 32.768kHz LSE crystals are started at boot but nothing
+is clocked from them yet. If a crystal does not start, the LED blinks before USB comes up, then the
+firmware carries on normally:
+
+| Blinks | Meaning                     |
+| ------ | --------------------------- |
+| 3      | HSE (25MHz) did not start   |
+| 2      | LSE (32.768kHz) did not start |
+
+With both failed, the HSE blinks come first, then the LSE blinks. Debug builds (`-Ddebug_output=true`)
+also log a warning.
+
+## Pinout
+
+| Function    | Pin  | Notes                                  |
+| ----------- | ---- | -------------------------------------- |
+| TCK/SWCLK   | PB13 | also external SPI SCLK                 |
+| TMS/SWDIO   | PB12 | also external SPI nCS                  |
+| TDI         | PB15 | also external SPI PICO                 |
+| TDO         | PB14 | also external SPI POCI                 |
+| nRST        | PA15 | open drain, internal pull-up           |
+| SWO         | PA1  | TIM5_CH2 / UART4_RX                    |
+| UART1 TX/RX | PA2/PA3   | USART2                            |
+| UART2 TX/RX | PA9/PA10  | USART1                            |
+| USB D-/D+   | PA11/PA12 | no VBUS sense                     |
+| LED         | PC13 | active low                             |
+| Flash nCS/CLK/DO/DI | PA4/PA5/PA6/PA7 | SPI1, U3 footprint |
+| HSE         | PH0/PH1   | 25MHz crystal                     |
+| LSE         | PC14/PC15 | 32.768kHz crystal                 |
+
+PA13/PA14 (SWDIO/SWCLK) on the 4-pin header debug the probe itself.
+
+## Building
+
+```sh
+meson setup build --cross-file=cross-file/weact-u585.ini
+meson compile -C build
+```
+
+This produces `build/blackmagic_weact_u585_firmware.{elf,bin}`.
+
+## Flashing
+
+Enter the ST ROM DFU bootloader (USB ID 0483:df11) by one of:
+
+- holding BOOT0 while pressing and releasing NRST
+- a DFU detach request to the running probe: `dfu-util -d 1d50:6018 -e`
+
+then:
+
+```sh
+dfu-util -a 0 -s 0x08000000:leave -D build/blackmagic_weact_u585_firmware.bin
+```
+
+On Windows, STM32CubeProgrammer installs the WinUSB driver the ROM bootloader needs and can also
+be used to flash the `.bin`.
